          "start_line": 672
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1351,
          "source_id": "TICKETS",
          "start_line": 1338
        }
      ],
      "text": "For ticketed work, resolve the current ticket through the Product Definition binding: the ticket is the durable work-state authority for that unit, while governing law and current workspace evidence retain their own authority. Derive execution from its admitted scope, linked governing inputs, results, residuals and continuation state. Where the selected law permits a sprint-local or run carrier, use that sufficient carrier. Comments, boards, indexes, prompts, handoffs and generated summaries are projections; recency or repetition gives them no competing authority. Contradiction among the ticket, required milestones, current goals or cited acceptance evidence withholds dependent closure. No extra ticket, registry or approval follows.",
      "unknowns": [],
      "when": {
        "all": [],
        "any": []
      }
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "depends_on": [
        "W01",
        "W02",
        "W34"
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "id": "W37",
      "kind": "obligation",
      "precedence": [],
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "end_line": 937,
          "source_id": "ACTIVATION",
          "start_line": 693
        }
      ],
      "text": "Construct the next decision context from the exact subject, outcome, material relations and selected basis. If required closure or projection is unresolved, return closure_unresolved before proceeding. Preserve excluded, external, unresolved, translated and invalidation-sensitive seams; omit irrelevant material, not material obligations. Retain a required body or qualified resolvable reference that preserves subject, basis, assessment standing, provenance, active obligation/version and invalidators; a candidate pointer or typed annotation alone proves no sufficiency. Acquire exact declared inputs read-only. Use a current sufficient derived surface or enter deciding source owners when it is stale, missing or insufficient; a candidate or selector cannot replace the selected operative basis. Render current obligations, proof expectations and fallback conditions without giving the prompt authority or importing historical workarounds that current law no longer needs.",
      "unknowns": [],
      "when": {
        "all": [],
        "any": []
      }
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "depends_on": [
        "W37"
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
      "id": "W38",
      "kind": "obligation",
      "precedence": [],
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "end_line": 937,
          "source_id": "ACTIVATION",
          "start_line": 693
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1680,
          "source_id": "ACTIVATION",
          "start_line": 1627
        }
      ],
      "text": "Where the activation declares a context capacity, measure the selected context before reading it in the declared unit over the selected execution boundary; record size, capacity and comparison. A measured-body fit covers only that boundary. Complete active inputs or a supported bound including host-supplied context are needed for the whole-step fit judgment; otherwise retain indeterminate unless evidence such as measured excess falsifies it. Keep starting bytes, cumulative acquisition including rereads, and the bound held at once distinct. Where no context capacity is declared, impose no universal measurement gate. If context does not fit, lawfully refine, sequence, compress with a recorded preservation argument, select a capable actor under the applicable grant, or return out_of_frame. Never silently omit material obligations, narrow the required predicate or enlarge another owner's envelope. Fit establishes neither adequate attention, task success nor authority.",
      "unknowns": [],
      "when": {
        "all": [],
        "any": []
      }
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "depends_on": [
        "W03",
        "W05",
        "W36"
      ],
      "exceptions": [],
